    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm finalizing the catering for a 500-person corporate gala for a law firm next week. We just got a bunch of last-minute updates: we have about 12 people with severe peanut allergies and another 8 who are strictly vegan. What's the best way to communicate this to the kitchen staff so nothing gets mixed up, and how should we handle the buffet labeling so guests can identify their food safely? Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Notify the kitchen staff of these last-minute dietary requirements succinctly by creating an updated ingredients list that excludes all products with nuts and includes a note about the vegan meals. For buffet labeling, use clear, bold fonts for the categories and individual allergens or include color-coded tags: green for vegan and red for nut-free. Moreover, encourage the servers to double-check each dish for these two categories during service. This will help guests easily navigate the food options, ensuring everyone can enjoy the event safely.",
      "source": "target",
