    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds like a solid start. One thing I'm worried about is the staff actually following through during the rush. A lot of the catering crew are new or temp staff. Do you have any advice on how to create a formal 'protocol' sheet or something I could hand them so they feel a sense of responsibility to not mess up the allergy orders?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! You could draft a ‘Safety and Order Protocol’ document that highlights the importance of adhering to the dietary restrictions due to severe allergies and for maintaining professionalism and safety standards. Include sections in the document that outline clear instructions on identifying allergen-free and vegan items, how to communicate specifically with guests regarding food concerns, and defined roles and responsibilities if you have a team for the event. Make it authoritative yet sensitive to the stress of a last-minute switch, reinforcing that everyone's safety is paramount. Staff should be asked to sign the document as a commitment to follow the protocol, possibly with a statement of understanding or a pledge. Consider confirming that all the temp and new hires read and understand the protocols before they start work the day of the event.",
